| flagged | attribution |
| --- | --- |
| 1 new reboot, `2026-10-27 20:52:38 Expected CLI(user request)` | **mine** — the `reload` of §N2, issued at 09:52:39 NZDT = 20:52:39 UTC. `Expected`, and it names the CLI as the cause |
| 34 new "kernel" lines, all stamped `2026 Oct 27 20:53:10` | **mine** — the boot that reload caused, 32 seconds later. They are ordinary boot messages: `Linux version 6.12.110`, `KASLR disabled due to lack of seed`, `Malformed early option 'loglevel'`, `Kernel command line: ...`, `GIC: Adjusting CPU interface base`, `SCSI subsystem initialized`, `mv_xor_v2 ... Marvell Version 2 XOR driver`. **No crash, no oops, no panic, no daemon restart** |
| exception log not None | **pre-existing** — the snmpd SIGSEGV of 2026-10-22 23:49:18, byte-identical to the before sample and five days older than this run. The documented dirty baseline of §3c |
| memory free −2608 kB | 0.03%. One case cannot show a leak and this log does not claim one |
| 3 `local6.warning startup-config:` lines | **mine, and they are evidence, not a fault** — the device's own record of the three config lines secure mode rejected at boot (§N3 ii) |

**Reboot reconciliation, the whole run.** `show reboot history` at the end holds exactly **two**
new entries over the before sample, and both are mine:

    2026-10-27 21:06:14 Expected   CLI(user request)    <- the disable reload (10:06:16 NZDT)
    2026-10-27 20:52:38 Expected   CLI(user request)    <- the enable  reload (09:52:39 NZDT)
    2026-10-22 23:55:56 Unexpected System reboot        <- pre-existing, unchanged

**No unexpected reboot occurred during this run.** The only `Unexpected` entry is the one that
was already there. The run is labelled **clean**.

(Method note, §10.3: a case that deliberately reboots will always trip this tool's DIRTY
verdict, because its matcher cannot tell a boot-time kernel message from a crash. The right
response is attribution, not alarm.)


